{"name":"Sprinkled With Dew","hex":"#cfecee","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sprinkled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of sprinkle"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sprinkled"},{"term":"with","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Against.","In the company of; alongside, close to; near to."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Along, together with others, in a group, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/with"},{"term":"dew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any moisture from the atmosphere condensed by cool bodies upon their surfaces.","Moisture in the air that settles on plants, etc in the morning or evening, resulting in drops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wet with, or as if with, dew; to moisten.","To deposit dew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dew"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dew","blocks":[{"text":"Dew is water in the form of droplets that appears on thin, exposed objects in the morning or evening due to condensation. \nAs the exposed surface cools by radiating its heat, atmospheric moisture condenses at a rate greater than that at which it can evaporate, resulting in the formation of water droplets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_drop_of_dew_on_a_clover.jpg/330px-A_drop_of_dew_on_a_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dew","wikidata":"Q41097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Dew_Formed_on_the_Surface_of_Strawberry_Leafs.jpg/500px-Dew_Formed_on_the_Surface_of_Strawberry_Leafs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Dew_Formed_on_the_Surface_of_Strawberry_Leafs.jpg/1280px-Dew_Formed_on_the_Surface_of_Strawberry_Leafs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_